    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "Suppose an electron is attracted towards the origin by a force $k/r$ where '$k$' is a constant and '$r$' is the distance of the electron from the origin. By applying Bohr model to this system, the radius of the $n^{\\text{th}}$ orbital of the electron is found to be '$r_n$' and the kinetic energy of the electron to be $T_n$. Then which of the following is true?",
