    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "A doubly ionised $\\text{Li}$ atom is excited from its ground state($n = 1$) to $n = 3$ state. The wavelengths of the spectral lines are given by $\\lambda_{32}$, $\\lambda_{31}$ and $\\lambda_{21}$. The ratio $\\lambda_{32}/\\lambda_{31}$ and $\\lambda_{21}/\\lambda_{31}$ are, respectively",
    "options": [
      "$8.1, 0.67$",
      "$8.1, 1.2$",
      "$6.4, 1.2$",
      "$6.4, 0.67$"
    ],
    "correct_index": 2,
    "correct_indices": [
      2
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = R\\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$ where $\\mathrm{R} = \\text{Rydberg constant}$. $\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{32}} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{3^2}\\right) = \\frac{5}{36} \\Rightarrow \\lambda_{32} = \\frac{36}{5}$\n\nSimilarly, solving for $\\lambda_{31}$ and $\\lambda_{21}$, $\\lambda_{31} = \\frac{9}{8}$, $\\lambda_{21} = \\frac{4}{3} \\therefore \\frac{\\lambda_{32}}{\\lambda_{31}} = 6.4$, $\\frac{\\lambda_{21}}{\\lambda_{31}} \\simeq 1.2$",
