    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$\\mathrm{E} = \\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda} \\Rightarrow \\lambda = \\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\mathrm{E}} = \\frac{6.62 \\times 10^{-34} \\times 3 \\times 10^{8}}{12.5 \\times 1.6 \\times 10^{-19}} = 993\\text{ \\AA}$$\n\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = \\mathrm{R}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_{1}^{2}} - \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_{2}^{2}}\\right) \\quad \\left(\\text{where Rydberg constant }, \\mathrm{R} = 1.097 \\times 10^{7}\\right) \\text{ or,}$$\n\n$$\\frac{1}{993 \\times 10^{-10}} = 1.097 \\times 10^{7}\\left(\\frac{1}{1^{2}} - \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_{2}^{2}}\\right)$$\n\nSolving we get $\\mathrm{n}_{2} = 3$.\n\nTotal number of spectral lines $= \\frac{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}-1)}{2} = \\frac{3(3-1)}{2} = 3$\n\nTwo lines in Lyman series for $\\mathrm{n}_{1} = 1, \\mathrm{n}_{2} = 2$ and $\\mathrm{n}_{1} = 1, \\mathrm{n}_{2} = 3$ and one in Balmer series for $\\mathrm{n}_{1} = 2, \\mathrm{n}_{2} = 3$.",
