    "solution": "For radiation, we know that\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = RZ^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$$\n$$\\therefore \\lambda \\propto \\frac{1}{Z^2}$$\n$$\\lambda_1 \\propto \\frac{1}{1}$$\n$$\\lambda_2 \\propto \\frac{1}{1}$$\n$$\\lambda_3 \\propto \\frac{1}{4}$$\n$$\\lambda_4 \\propto \\frac{1}{9}$$\n$$\\therefore \\lambda_1 = \\lambda_2 = 4\\lambda_3 = 9\\lambda_4$$",
