    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "If one were to apply the Bohr model to a particle of mass '$m$' and charge '$q$' moving in a plane under the influence of a magnetic field 'B', the energy of the charged particle in the $n^{\\text{th}}$ level will be:",
    "options": [
      "$n\\left(\\dfrac{hqB}{\\pi m}\\right)$",
      "$n\\left(\\dfrac{hqB}{4\\pi m}\\right)$",
      "$n\\left(\\dfrac{hqB}{2\\pi m}\\right)$",
      "$n\\left(\\dfrac{hqB}{8\\pi m}\\right)$"
    ],
    "correct_index": 1,
    "correct_indices": [
      1
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "For a charge $q$ moving in a uniform magnetic field $B$:\n\n$$qVB = \\frac{mv^2}{R} \\Rightarrow mv^2 = qVBR \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{2}mv^2 = \\frac{qVBR}{2} \\Rightarrow \\text{Energy} = \\frac{qVBR}{2} \\quad \\text{--- (1)}$$\n\nBy Bohr's quantization condition,\n$$\\text{Angular momentum } L = n\\frac{h}{2\\pi} \\Rightarrow mvR = \\frac{nh}{2\\pi} \\Rightarrow vR = \\frac{nh}{2\\pi m} \\quad \\text{--- (2)}$$\n\nPut (2) in (1):\n$$\\Rightarrow \\text{Energy} = \\frac{qB}{2}\\left(\\frac{nh}{2\\pi m}\\right) = \\frac{qBnh}{4\\pi m} = n\\left(\\frac{hqB}{4\\pi m}\\right)$$",
