    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Let us assume that the electron in the lithium-ion is knocked off from the $n^{th}$ energy level, then\n\n$$R(Z_H)^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{2^2}\\right) = R\\frac{(Z_{Li})^2}{n^2}$$\n\n$$R(1)^2 \\times \\frac{3}{4} = R(3)^2 \\left[\\frac{1}{n^2}\\right]$$\n\n$$\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{9}{n^2}$$\n\n$$n = \\sqrt{12} \\approx 3.5$$\n\nHence the least quantum number must be 4.",
