    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Let velocity before collision $v$ from momentum conservation $mv = (m + m)v^1$\n\n$$v^1 = \\frac{v}{2}$$\n\n$$\\text{Loss in K.E.} = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2 - \\frac{1}{2}(2m)\\left(\\frac{v}{2}\\right)^2$$\n$$= \\frac{1}{4}mv^2$$\n\n$\\text{K.E.}$ lost is used to jump from $1^{\\text{st}}$ orbit to $2^{\\text{nd}}$ orbit $\\Delta K.E. = 10.2\\text{ eV}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{4}mv^2 = 10.2$$\n\n$$\\frac{1}{2}mv^2 = 2 \\times 10.2 = 20.4\\text{ eV}$$",
