    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$v \\propto \\frac{z}{n}$$\n\n$$r \\propto \\frac{n^2}{z}$$\n\n$$B = \\frac{\\mu I}{2R}$$\n\n$$I = \\frac{e}{T} = \\frac{e}{\\left(\\frac{2\\pi R}{v}\\right)} = \\frac{e}{2\\pi} \\frac{v}{R}$$\n\n$$B = \\frac{\\mu_0}{2} \\frac{e}{2\\pi} \\frac{v}{R^2}$$\n\n$$B = \\frac{\\mu_0 e}{4\\pi} \\frac{z}{n \\left(\\frac{n^2}{z}\\right)^2}$$\n\n$$B = \\frac{\\mu_0 e}{4\\pi} \\frac{z^3}{n^5}$$\n\n$$B \\propto n^{-5}.$$",
