    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "For $\\text{H-atom}$ ($n = 1$)\n\n$$\\frac{mv^2}{r} = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0}\\frac{e^2}{r^2} \\dots (1)$$\n\n$$mvr = \\frac{h}{2\\pi} \\dots (2)$$\n\nOn squaring (2):\n\n$$m^2 v^2 r^2 = \\frac{h^2}{4\\pi^2}$$\n\nOn dividing both sides by $r^3$:\n\n$$\\frac{m^2 v^2}{r} = \\frac{h^2}{4\\pi^2 r^3} \\Rightarrow \\frac{v^2}{r} = \\frac{h^2}{4\\pi^2 r^3 m^2}$$\n\n$$\\text{Acceleration} = \\frac{h^2}{4\\pi^2 r^3 m^2}$$",
