    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "An electron from various excited states of hydrogen atom emit radiation to come to the ground state. Let $\\lambda_n, \\lambda_g$ be the de Broglie wavelength of the electron in the $n^{\\text{th}}$ state and the ground state respectively. Let $\\Lambda_n$ be the wavelength of the emitted photon in the transition from the $n^{\\text{th}}$ state to the ground state. For large $n$, ($A$, $B$ are constants)",
    "options": [
      "$\\Lambda_n^2 \\approx \\lambda$",
      "$\\Lambda_n \\approx A + \\frac{B}{\\lambda_n^2}$",
      "$\\Lambda_n \\approx A + B\\lambda_n$",
      "$\\Lambda_n^2 \\approx A + B\\lambda_n^2$"
    ],
    "correct_index": 1,
    "correct_indices": [
      1
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$2\\pi r = n\\lambda_n$$\n$$\\lambda_n = \\frac{2\\pi r}{n}$$\n$$\\because r = r_o n^2$$\n$$\\lambda_n = \\frac{2\\pi}{n} r_o n^2 = n(2\\pi r_o) \\dots (i)$$\n\n$$\\frac{1}{\\Lambda_n} = R \\left\\{ \\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{n^2} \\right\\}$$\n$$\\Lambda_n = \\frac{1}{R} \\left\\{ 1 + \\frac{1}{n^2 - 1} \\right\\}$$\n$$\\Lambda_n = \\frac{1}{R} \\left\\{ 1 + \\frac{1}{n^2} \\right\\} \\dots (ii)$$\n\nfrom $(i)$ and $(ii)$,\n$$\\Lambda_n = \\frac{1}{R} \\left\\{ 1 + \\frac{4\\pi^2 r_o^2}{\\lambda_n^2} \\right\\} = A + \\frac{B}{\\lambda_n^2}$$",
