    "solution": "The energy is required to remove $\\mathrm{e^-}$ from singly ionized helium atom $= 54.4\\mathrm{ eV}$. The energy required to remove $\\mathrm{e^-}$ from a helium atom $= x\\mathrm{ eV}$, given $54.4\\mathrm{ eV} = 2.2x \\Rightarrow x = 24.73\\mathrm{ eV}$. The energy required to ionize helium atom $= 79.13\\mathrm{ eV} \\approx 79\\mathrm{ eV}$.",
