    "solution": "Energy required to remove $\\mathrm{e^-}$ from singly ionized helium atom $= \\frac{(13.6)Z^2}{1^2} = 54.4\\mathrm{ eV} \\ (\\because Z = 2)$\n\nEnergy required to remove $\\mathrm{e^-}$ from helium atom $= x\\mathrm{ eV}$\n\nAccording to question, $54.4\\mathrm{ eV} = 2.2x \\Rightarrow x = 24.73\\mathrm{ eV}$\n\nTherefore, energy required to ionize helium atom $= (54.4 + 24.73)\\mathrm{ eV} = 79.12\\mathrm{ eV}$",
