    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "(A) $\\text{Radius of muon} = \\frac{\\text{Radius of hydrogen}}{200}$\n$\\text{Radius of H atom} = r = \\frac{\\epsilon_0 n^2 h^2}{\\pi m e^2}$\n$\\text{Radius of muon} = r_\\mu = \\frac{\\epsilon_0 n^2 h^2}{\\pi \\times 200 m e^2}$\n$r_\\mu = \\frac{r}{200}$\n\n(B) Velocity relation given is wrong\n\n(C) Ionization energy in $e^- \\text{H}$ atom $E = \\frac{+m e^4}{8 \\epsilon_0^2 n^2 h^2}$\n$E_\\mu = \\frac{200 m e^4}{8 \\epsilon_0^2 n^2 h^2} = 200E$\n\n(D) Momentum of $\\text{H}$-atom $mvr = \\frac{nh}{2\\pi}$\n\nHence (A), (C), (D) are correct.",
