    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$\\frac{\\lambda_N}{\\lambda_a} = \\frac{E_a}{E_N}$, where $E_a$ and $E_N$ are energies of photons from atom and nucleus respectively. $E_N$ is of the order of $\\text{MeV}$ and $E_a$ in few $\\text{eV}$. So, $\\frac{\\lambda_N}{\\lambda_a} = 10^{-6}$.",
