    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "When electron pass through the mercury vapor, it losses some of its energy. The loss in $KE$ of electron\n$= (5.6 - 0.7) eV = 4.9 eV$\n\n$\\therefore$ energy of radiation emitted $= 4.9 eV$\n\n$\\therefore$ wavelength of radiation, $\\lambda = \\frac{1.24 \\times 10^4}{4.9} \\text{ \\AA} \\approx 250 nm$",
