    "solution": "$E = 13.6 \\left(\\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{2^2}\\right) eV \\dots (1)$\n\nFor Helium:\n$E = 13.6(2)^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right) eV \\dots (2)$\n\nFrom equation (1) and (2)\n$13.6 \\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) = 13.6 (4) \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$\n\n$\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2} = \\frac{3}{16}$\n\nFrom option, $n_1 = 2$ and $n_2 = 4$ are satisfying the equation.",
