    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "An excited $\\mathrm{He}^{+}$ ion emits two photons in succession, with wavelengths $108.5\\,nm$ and $30.4\\,nm$ in making a transition to the ground state. The quantum number $n$, corresponding to its initial excited state is\n\n(for a photon of wavelength $\\lambda$, energy $E = \\frac{1240\\,eV}{\\lambda(in\\,nm)}$)",
    "options": [
      "$n = 6$",
      "$n = 5$",
      "$n = 7$",
      "$n = 4$"
    ],
    "correct_index": 1,
    "correct_indices": [
      1
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$E_1 = \\frac{1240}{\\lambda_1} = \\frac{1240}{108.5} \\approx 11.43\\,eV$$\n$$E_2 = \\frac{1240}{\\lambda_2} = \\frac{1240}{30.4} \\approx 40.79\\,eV$$\n$$E_{Total} = E_1 + E_2 = 52.22\\,eV$$\n$$52.22 = 13.6(2)^2 \\left[1 - \\frac{1}{n^2}\\right]$$\n$$52.22 = 54.4\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{n^2}\\right)$$\n$$0.96 = 1 - \\frac{1}{n^2}$$\n$$\\frac{1}{n^2} = 0.04$$\n$$n^2 = \\frac{1}{0.04} = \\frac{100}{4} = 25$$\n$$n = 5$$",
    "image_url": null,
