    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 486,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = RZ^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$$\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_1} = R(1)^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{4^2}\\right) = \\frac{3R}{16}$$\n$$\\frac{\\lambda_2}{\\lambda_1} = \\frac{20}{27}$$\n$$\\lambda_2 = \\frac{20}{27} \\times 6561\\text{ \\AA} = 4860\\text{ \\AA}$$\n$$= 486\\text{ nm}$$",
