    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "In the line spectra of hydrogen atom, difference between the largest and the shortest wavelengths of the Lyman series is $305\\,\\text{\\AA}$. The corresponding difference for the Paschan series in $\\text{\\AA}$ is:______",
    "options": [],
    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 10553.14,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{\\min}} = R(1) = R ; n = \\infty \\text{ to } 1$$\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{\\max}} = R\\left\\{1 - \\frac{1}{4}\\right\\} = \\frac{3R}{4} ; n = 2 \\text{ to } 1$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\lambda_{\\max} - \\lambda_{\\min} = \\frac{4}{3R} - \\frac{1}{R}$$\n$$304 = \\frac{1}{3R} \\dots (a)$$\nPaschen : $\\frac{1}{\\lambda'_{\\min}} = R\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right)$\nand $\\frac{1}{\\lambda'_{\\max}} = R\\left(\\frac{1}{9} - \\frac{1}{16}\\right) = \\frac{7R}{16 \\times 9}$\n$$\\lambda'_{\\max} - \\lambda'_{\\min} = \\frac{16 \\times 9}{7R} - \\frac{9}{R} = \\frac{81}{7R} \\dots (b)$$\n$$\\frac{(b)}{(a)} = \\frac{x}{3 \\times 304} = \\frac{81}{7}$$\n$$\\Rightarrow x = 10553.14$$",
    "image_url": null,
    "solution_image_url": null,
    "starter_code": null,
