    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "The first three spectral lines of $H$-atom in the Balmer series are given $\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2, \\lambda_3$ considering the Bohr atomic model, the wave lengths of first and third spectral lines $\\left(\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_3}\\right)$ are related by a factor of approximately $x \\times 10^{-1}$. The value of $x$, to the nearest integer, is _______.",
    "options": [],
    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 15,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_1} = Rz^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{3^2}\\right)$$\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_1} = Rz^2 \\frac{5}{36} \\text{ ...(i)}$$\n\nFor $3^{\\text{rd}}$ line\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_3} = Rz^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{5^2}\\right)$$\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_3} = Rz^2 \\frac{21}{100} \\text{ ...(ii)}$$\n\n$(ii) \\div (i)$\n$$\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_3} = \\frac{21}{100} \\times \\frac{36}{5} = 1.512 = 15.12 \\times 10^{-1}$$\n$$x \\approx 15$$",
    "image_url": null,
