    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Energy of $H$-atom is $E = -13.6 Z^2 / n^2$ for $H$-atom $Z = 1$ and for ground state, $n = 1$\n$$\\Rightarrow E = -13.6 \\times \\frac{1^2}{1^2} = -13.6\\text{ eV}$$\n\nNow for carbon atom (single ionised), $Z = 6$\n$$E = -13.6 \\frac{Z^2}{n^2} = -13.6\\text{ (given)}$$\n$$\\Rightarrow n^2 = 6^2 \\Rightarrow n = 6$$",
