    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "In Bohr's atomic model, the electron is assumed to revolve in a circular orbit of radius $0.5\\,\\text{\\AA}$. If the speed of electron is $2.2 \\times 10^6\\,ms^{-1}$. Then the current associated with the electron will be ______ $\\times 10^{-2}\\,mA$. $\\left[\\text{Take } \\pi \\text{ as } \\frac{22}{7}\\right]$",
    "options": [],
    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 112,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Time taken to revolve in circular orbit is $$T = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\omega} = \\frac{2\\pi r}{v} = \\frac{2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 5 \\times 10^{-11}}{2.2 \\times 10^6} = \\frac{10}{7} \\times 10^{-16}\\,s$$\n\nNow, current associated with the electron is $$I = \\frac{e}{T} = \\frac{1.6 \\times 10^{-19}}{\\frac{10}{7} \\times 10^{-16}} = 1.12 \\times 10^{-3}\\,A$$\n$$\\Rightarrow I = 1.12\\,mA$$\n\nHence, the current is $112 \\times 10^{-2}\\,mA$.",
    "image_url": null,
    "solution_image_url": null,
    "starter_code": null,
    "test_cases": null,
    "language": null,
    "assertion_text": null,
    "reason_text": null,
