    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "The $K_\\alpha$ X-ray of molybdenum has wavelength $0.071\\text{ nm}$. If the energy of a molybdenum atom with a $K$ electron knocked out is $27.5\\text{ keV}$, the energy of this atom when an $L$ electron is knocked out will be $\\text{______ } \\text{keV}$. (Round off to the nearest integer ) [ $h = 4.14 \\times 10^{-15}\\text{ eV s}, c = 3 \\times 10^8\\text{ ms}^{-1}$ ]",
    "options": [],
    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 10,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$E_{k_\\alpha} = E_k - E_L$$\n\n$$\\frac{hc}{\\lambda_{k_\\alpha}} = E_k - E_L$$\n\n$$E_L = E_k - \\frac{hc}{\\lambda_{k_\\alpha}}$$\n\n$$= 27.5\\text{ keV} - \\frac{12.42 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ eV m}}{0.071 \\times 10^{-9}\\text{ m}}$$\n\n$$E_L = (27.5 - 17.5)\\text{ keV}$$\n\n$$= 10\\text{ keV}$$",
    "image_url": null,
