    "solution": "According to Bohr's postulates, angular momentum of an electron in an orbit is given by,\n\n$L = mvr = \\frac{nh}{2\\pi}$\n\nTherefore, linear momentum $p = \\frac{L}{r} = \\frac{nh}{2\\pi r}$",
