    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "$\\frac{x}{x + 4}$ is the ratio of energies of photons produced due to transition of an electron of hydrogen atom from its\n(i) third permitted energy level to the second level and\n(ii) the highest permitted energy level to the second permitted level.\nThe value of $x$ will be",
    "options": [],
    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 5,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Energy of a photon released in transition of electron in hydrogen atom is given by,\n$$E = 13.6 \\left( \\frac{1}{{n_2}^2} - \\frac{1}{{n_1}^2} \\right) eV$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{E_1}{E_2} = \\frac{13.6 \\left( \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{9} \\right)}{13.6 \\left( \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{\\infty} \\right)} = \\frac{x}{x + 4} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{9}}{\\frac{1}{4}} = \\frac{x}{x + 4}$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{5}{9} = \\frac{x}{x + 4}$$\n$$\\Rightarrow 5x + 20 = 9x$$\n$$\\Rightarrow x = 5$$",
