    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "For hydrogen atom, $\\lambda_1$ and $\\lambda_2$ are the wavelengths corresponding to the transitions $1$ and $2$ respectively as shown in figure. The ratio of $\\lambda_1$ and $\\lambda_2$ is $\\frac{x}{32}$. The value of $x$ is ______.",
    "options": [],
    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 27,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Wavelength corresponding to the photon emitted in transition $n = 3$ to $n = 1$ is $\\frac{1}{\\lambda_1} = R\\left(\\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{3^2}\\right) = \\frac{8R}{9}$ ....(1)\n\nWavelength corresponding to the photon emitted for transition $n = 2$ to $n = 1$ is $\\frac{1}{\\lambda_2} = R\\left(\\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{2^2}\\right) = \\frac{3R}{4}$ ....(2)\n\n$\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_2} = \\frac{3R}{4} \\times \\frac{9}{8R} = \\frac{27}{32}$\n\nHence, the value of $x = 27$.",
