    "correct_index": 1,
    "correct_indices": [
      1
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "As we know, radius of hydrogen like atom $r \\propto \\frac{n^2}{Z}$.\n\nTherefore,\n$$\\frac{r_2}{r_3} = \\left(\\frac{n_2}{n_3}\\right)^2$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{R}{r_3} = \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2$$\n$$\\Rightarrow r_3 = \\frac{9}{4} R$$\n$$= 2.25 R$$",
