    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Using Rydberg's formula,\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = RZ^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$$\nFor the lowest wavelength in Lyman series, $n_1 = 1, n_2 = \\infty$.\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = RZ^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{\\infty^2}\\right) = RZ^2$$\nFor Balmer series, $n_1 = 2, n_2 = \\infty$\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda'} = RZ^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{\\infty^2}\\right) = \\frac{RZ^2}{4}$$\nSo,\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda'} = \\frac{1}{4\\lambda} \\Rightarrow \\lambda' = 4 \\times 917\\text{ Å} = 3668\\text{ Å}$$",
