    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "A monochromatic light is incident on a hydrogen sample in ground state. Hydrogen atoms absorb a fraction of light and subsequently emit radiation of six different wavelengths. The frequency of incident light is $x \\times 10^{15}\\text{ Hz}$. The value of $x$ is _____\n\n(Given $h = 4.25 \\times 10^{-15}\\text{ eV s}$)",
