    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 3,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Let the higher state be $n$.\nThe number of wavelengths emitted is given by,\n$$\\frac{n(n - 1)}{2} = 6 \\Rightarrow n^2 - n - 12 = 0 \\Rightarrow (n - 4)(n + 3) = 0 \\Rightarrow n = 4$$\nFor hydrogen atom,\n$$h\\nu = 13.6 \\left(\\frac{1}{1} - \\frac{1}{16}\\right) = \\left(13.6 \\times \\frac{15}{16}\\right)\\text{ eV} \\Rightarrow \\nu = \\frac{E}{h} = \\frac{13.6 \\times 15 \\times 1.6 \\times 10^{-19}}{16 \\times 6.62 \\times 10^{-34}} = 3 \\times 10^{15}\\text{ Hz}$$",
