    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "The radius of third stationary orbit of electron for Bohr's atom is $R$. The radius of fourth stationary orbit will be:",
    "options": [
      "$\\frac{4}{3} R$",
      "$\\frac{16}{9} R$",
      "$\\frac{3}{4} R$",
      "$\\frac{9}{16} R$"
    ],
    "correct_index": 1,
    "correct_indices": [
      1
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "From Bohr's atomic model, it follows that\n$$r_n = \\frac{n^2}{Z} r_1 \\dots (1)$$\nFollowing equation (1), it can be written that\n$$\\frac{r_4}{r_3} = \\frac{4^2}{3^2} \\Rightarrow r_4 = \\frac{16}{9} R$$",
