    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 17,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "According to the energy level diagram, the difference in energy between the two states is given by\n$$\\Delta E = -3.4 \\text{ eV} - (-13.6 \\text{ eV}) = 10.2 \\text{ eV}$$\n\nThe formula to calculate the recoil speed is given by\n$$v = \\frac{\\Delta E}{mc} \\quad \\dots (1)$$\n\nFrom equation (1), it follows that\n$$v = \\frac{10.2 \\text{ eV} \\times \\frac{1.6 \\times 10^{-19} \\text{ J}}{1 \\text{ eV}}}{1.6 \\times 10^{-27} \\text{ kg} \\times 3 \\times 10^8 \\text{ ms}^{-1}} = 3.4 \\text{ ms}^{-1} = \\frac{17}{5} \\text{ ms}^{-1}$$\n\nTherefore, $x = 17$.",
