    "chapter": "Atomic",
    "chapter_id": 146,
    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "An electron revolving in $n^{\\text{th}}$ Bohr orbit has magnetic moment $\\mu_n$. If $\\mu_n \\propto n^x$, the value of $x$ is:",
    "options": [
      "2",
      "1",
      "3",
      "0"
    ],
    "correct_index": 1,
    "correct_indices": [
      1
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "Magnetic moment of electron is given by, $\\mu_n = \\frac{ehn}{4\\pi m_e}$.\n\nClearly, $\\mu_n \\propto n^1$. Therefore, $x = 1$.",
    "image_url": null,
    "solution_image_url": null,
    "starter_code": null,
    "test_cases": null,
