    "correct_index": 0,
    "correct_indices": [
      0
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "For Lyman series:\n\nFor first member, $\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = \\frac{13.6Z^2}{hc}\\left[\\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{2^2}\\right]$ ..... (i)\n\nFor second member, $\\frac{1}{\\lambda'} = \\frac{13.6Z^2}{hc}\\left[\\frac{1}{1^2} - \\frac{1}{3^2}\\right]$ ..... (ii)\n\nOn dividing (i) and (ii), we get\n$$\\lambda' = \\frac{27}{32}\\lambda$$",
