    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$$\\text{F} = \\frac{k(\\text{Ze})(e)}{r^2} = \\frac{mv^2}{r}$$\n\n$$\\text{KE} = \\frac{1}{2}mv^2 = \\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{K}(\\text{Ze})(e)}{r}$$\n\n$$\\text{PE} = -\\frac{\\text{K}(\\text{Ze})(e)}{r}$$\n\n$$\\text{TE} = \\frac{\\text{K}(\\text{Ze})(e)}{2r} - \\frac{\\text{K}(\\text{Ze})(e)}{r} = \\frac{-\\text{K}(\\text{Ze})(e)}{2r}$$\n\n$$\\text{TE} = \\frac{\\text{PE}}{2}$$\n\n$$2\\text{TE} = \\text{PE}$$",
