    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "numerical",
    "question_text": "The shortest wavelength of the spectral lines in the Lyman series of hydrogen spectrum is $915\\text{ \\AA}$.\n\nThe longest wavelength of spectral lines in the Balmer series will be _____ $\\text{\\AA}$.",
    "options": [],
    "correct_index": null,
    "correct_indices": [],
    "numeric_answer": 6588,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0.05,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 0,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "For shortest wavelength in Lyman series ($n = \\infty$ to $n = 1$):\n$$\\frac{hc}{\\lambda} = 13.6 \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$$\n$$\\frac{hc}{\\lambda_0} = 13.6 (1)$$\n\nFor longest wavelength in Balmer series ($n = 3$ to $n = 2$):\n$$\\frac{hc}{\\lambda_1} = 13.6 \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{3^2}\\right)$$\n$$\\frac{hc}{\\lambda_1} = 13.6 \\left(\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{9}\\right) = 13.6 \\times \\left(\\frac{5}{36}\\right)$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{13.6 \\lambda_0}{\\lambda_1} = 13.6 \\times \\frac{5}{36}$$\n$$\\lambda_1 = \\frac{\\lambda_0 \\times 36}{5} = \\frac{915 \\times 36}{5} = 6588\\text{ \\AA}$$",
