    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = R z^2 \\left( \\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2} \\right)$\n\nFor shortest wavelength of Lyman series ($n_1 = 1, n_2 = \\infty$):\n$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{\\text{L}}} = R z^2 \\left( \\frac{1}{1^2} \\right)$\n\nFor shortest wavelength of Balmer series ($n_1 = 2, n_2 = \\infty$):\n$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{\\text{B}}} = R z^2 \\left( \\frac{1}{2^2} \\right)$\n\n$\\frac{\\lambda_{\\text{B}}}{\\lambda_{\\text{L}}} = 4 : 1$",
