    "topic": "Atomic",
    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "For a hydrogen atom, the ratio of the largest wavelength of Lyman series to that of the Balmer series is.",
    "options": [
      "$5 : 36$",
      "$5 : 27$",
      "$3 : 4$",
      "$27 : 5$"
    ],
    "correct_index": 1,
    "correct_indices": [
      1
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "For Lyman series (largest wavelength corresponds to transition from $n = 2$ to $n = 1$):\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_1} = R \\left[\\frac{1}{1} - \\frac{1}{4}\\right] = \\frac{3R}{4} \\implies \\lambda_1 = \\frac{4}{3R} \\quad \\dots (1)$$\n\nFor Balmer series (largest wavelength corresponds to transition from $n = 3$ to $n = 2$):\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_2} = R \\left[\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{9}\\right] = \\frac{5R}{36} \\implies \\lambda_2 = \\frac{36}{5R}$$\n\nThen,\n$$\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_2} = \\frac{4/(3R)}{36/(5R)} = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{5}{36} = \\frac{5}{27}$$",
    "image_url": "/uploads/atomic_physics/q136_diagram.png",
