    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "If an alpha particle with energy $7.7\\text{ MeV}$ is bombarded on a thin gold foil, the closest distance from nucleus it can reach is _____ $\\text{m}$. (Atomic number of gold $= 79$ and $\\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0} = 9 \\times 10^9$ in SI units)",
    "options": [
      "$3.85 \\times 10^{-16}$",
      "$3.85 \\times 10^{-14}$",
      "$2.95 \\times 10^{-16}$",
      "$2.95 \\times 10^{-14}$"
    ],
    "correct_index": 3,
    "correct_indices": [
      3
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "At closest approach, KE converts to PE:\n$$KE = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_0} \\times \\frac{(2e)(Ze)}{r_{\\text{min}}}$$\n$$r_{\\text{min}} = \\frac{9 \\times 10^9 \\times 2 \\times 79 \\times (1.6 \\times 10^{-19})^2}{7.7 \\times 10^6 \\times 1.6 \\times 10^{-19}}$$\n$$= \\frac{9 \\times 2 \\times 79 \\times 1.6 \\times 10^{-19}}{7.7} \\times 10^3$$\n$$= \\frac{2275.2}{7.7} \\times 10^{-16} = 2.95 \\times 10^{-14}\\text{ m}$$",
