    "solution": "A. Maximum wavelength of Lyman series ($n = 1$ to $n = 2$):\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = R\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{4}\\right) = \\frac{3R}{4}$$\n$$\\lambda = \\frac{4}{3R} \\text{ TRUE}$$\n\nB. The Balmer series lies in the visible region of the spectrum. TRUE\n\nC. Minimum wavelength of Paschen series ($n = 3$ to $n = \\infty$):\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda'} = R\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right)$$\n$$\\lambda' = \\frac{9}{R} \\text{ TRUE}$$\n\nD. Minimum wavelength of Lyman series ($n = 1$ to $n = \\infty$):\n$$\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = R(1)$$\n$$\\lambda = \\frac{1}{R}, \\text{ NOT } \\frac{5}{4R} \\text{ FALSE}$$\n\nSo A, B and C are correct.",
