    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "Two electrons are moving in orbits of two hydrogen like atoms with speeds $3 \\times 10^5\\text{ m/s}$ and $2.5 \\times 10^5\\text{ m/s}$ respectively. If the radii of these orbits are nearly same then the possible order of energy states are _____ respectively.",
    "options": [
      "8 and 10",
      "9 and 8",
      "10 and 12",
      "6 and 5"
    ],
    "correct_index": 3,
    "correct_indices": [
      3
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "For hydrogen-like atoms:\n$V \\propto \\frac{Z}{n}$ and $r \\propto \\frac{n^2}{Z}$\n\nThus $r \\propto \\frac{n}{V}$\n\nSince the radii are nearly the same:\n$\\frac{n_1}{V_1} = \\frac{n_2}{V_2}$\n\n$\\frac{n_1}{n_2} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{3 \\times 10^5}{2.5 \\times 10^5} = \\frac{6}{5}$\n\nPossible order of energy states is 6 and 5.",
