    "exam_type": "JEE",
    "question_type": "single",
    "question_text": "The ratio of momentum of the photons of the $1^{\\text{st}}$ and $2^{\\text{nd}}$ line of Balmer series of Hydrogen atoms is $\\alpha / \\beta$. The possible values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are:-",
    "options": [
      "27 and 20",
      "3 and 16",
      "5 and 36",
      "20 and 27"
    ],
    "correct_index": 3,
    "correct_indices": [
      3
    ],
    "numeric_answer": null,
    "numerical_tolerance": 0,
    "marks": 4,
    "negative_marks": 1,
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "status": "available",
    "solution": "The momentum of a photon is given by $p = \\frac{h}{\\lambda}$.\n\nFrom Rydberg's formula, the wave number is $\\frac{1}{\\lambda} = R \\left(\\frac{1}{n_1^2} - \\frac{1}{n_2^2}\\right)$.\n\nFor the first line of the Balmer series, the transition is from $n_2 = 3$ to $n_1 = 2$.\n$$p_1 = \\frac{h}{\\lambda_1} = hR \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{3^2}\\right) = hR \\left(\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{9}\\right) = \\frac{5hR}{36}$$\n\nFor the second line of the Balmer series, the transition is from $n_2 = 4$ to $n_1 = 2$.\n$$p_2 = \\frac{h}{\\lambda_2} = hR \\left(\\frac{1}{2^2} - \\frac{1}{4^2}\\right) = hR \\left(\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{16}\\right) = \\frac{3hR}{16}$$\n\nThe ratio of the momenta is:\n$$\\frac{p_1}{p_2} = \\frac{\\frac{5hR}{36}}{\\frac{3hR}{16}} = \\frac{5}{36} \\times \\frac{16}{3} = \\frac{20}{27}$$\n\nComparing with $\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta}$, the possible values are $\\alpha = 20$ and $\\beta = 27$.\n\nAnswer: 20 and 27",
